## 🚀 How to Run the Project

Follow these simple steps to run the backend API server and frontend client on your local machine.

### 1. Prerequisites
Ensure you have the following installed:
- **Node.js**: v18.0 or newer ([Download Node.js](https://nodejs.org/))
- **MongoDB**: Running locally at `mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017` or a cloud [MongoDB Atlas](https://www.mongodb.com/atlas) connection string.

---

### 2. Step-by-Step Setup

#### Step A: Start the Backend Server
Open a terminal in the project directory:

```bash
cd backend
npm install
npm run dev
```

- The API server will boot up at **`http://localhost:{{app.port}}`**
- Verify the server is running by opening: [http://localhost:{{app.port}}/api/health](http://localhost:{{app.port}}/api/health)

#### Step B: Start the Frontend Client
Open a **second terminal** window in the project directory:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

- The React client will start at **`http://localhost:{{app.clientPort}}`**
- Open **[http://localhost:{{app.clientPort}}](http://localhost:{{app.clientPort}})** in your web browser to start using the app!

