## 🎯 How to Use the Application

### 1. Dashboard Overview
Once you open `http://localhost:{{app.clientPort}}`:
- View high-level metric cards showing total counts for each entity.
- Monitor backend API connectivity and system status in real-time.

{{#if app.auth}}
### 2. Authentication
- Click **Register** on the top navigation bar to create a new user account.
- Sign in with your email and password. Your JWT session token is securely stored in `localStorage` and automatically attached to all subsequent API requests.
- Log out at any time using the user profile menu in the navigation bar.
{{/if}}

### 3. Managing Entities
Use the sidebar on the left to navigate to any entity section:
- **List View (`/entity`)**: View records in a clean tabular layout. Use the search input to filter items across string fields, and navigate with page controls.
- **Create New (`/entity/new`)**: Click the **New** button to open the type-aware form. Required fields are marked with an asterisk (*). Any related entities will automatically appear as selectable options in dropdown menus.
- **Detail View (`/entity/:id`)**: Click the eye icon to inspect complete record details, populated relationships, and creation/update timestamps.
- **Edit & Delete (`/entity/:id/edit`)**: Modify records in place or delete them with confirmation.

